---
<ul>
  <li><strong>Works on every screen.</strong> The responsive layout is easier to use on phones, tablets, and desktop computers.</li>
  <li><strong>Simpler navigation.</strong> A consistent, organized menu makes the collection easier to explore.</li>
  <li><strong>More accessible pages.</strong> Semantic structure, keyboard-friendly controls, readable contrast, and descriptive image text support more visitors.</li>
  <li><strong>Better ways to browse.</strong> People, places, heritage homes, events, and other records are organized into clear indexes.</li>
  <li><strong>Interactive discovery.</strong> Maps and timelines reveal geographic and chronological connections across the collection.</li>
  <li><strong>Connected history.</strong> Related people, places, and articles link to one another so visitors can follow a story across the archive.</li>
  <li><strong>Improved reading without losing the source.</strong> Selected articles offer carefully copy-edited text alongside the preserved original wording.</li>
  <li><strong>Built for preservation.</strong> Clean UTF-8 text, semantic HTML, structured metadata, and recorded source details make the archive easier to maintain and extend.</li>
</ul>
